(< λείπω), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨יֶתֶר⁩, also for ⁨שְׁאָר⁩, etc.;] ⟪the remaining⟫, ⟪the rest⟫,
⟪1.⟫ pl., οἱ λ.: c. subst., ⟦Matthew 25:11|Mt 25:11⟧, ⟦Acts 2:37|Ac 2:37⟧, ⟦Romans 1:13|Ro 1:13⟧, al.; absol., ⟦Matthew 22:6|Mt 22:6⟧, ⟦Mark 16:13|Mk 16:[13]⟧, ⟦Luke 24:10|Lk 24:10⟧, al.; οἱ λ. οἱ (Bl., § 47, 8), ⟦Acts 28:9|Ac 28:9⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 4:13|I Th 4:13⟧, ⟦Revelation 2:24|Re 2:24⟧; οἱ λ. τ. ἀνθρώπων (LS, s.v., ad. init.), ⟦Revelation 9:20|Re 9:20⟧; τὰ λ., ⟦Mark 4:19|Mk 4:19⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:2|Re 3:2⟧, al.
⟪2.⟫ Neut. sing. (acc. ref.), adverbially, τὸ λ.;
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪for the future⟫, ⟪henceforth⟫: ⟦Mark 14:41|Mk 14:41⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:29|I Co 7:29⟧ (Lft., Notes, 232 f.), ⟦Hebrews 10:13|He 10:13⟧; anarth. (Deiss., LAE, 17616, 1885, 20), ⟦Acts 27:20|Ac 27:20⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 4:8|II Ti 4:8⟧; τοῦ λ. (sc. χρόνου; LS, s.v.; M, Pr., 73; Bl., § 36, 13), ⟦Galatians 6:17|Ga 6:17⟧, ⟦Ephesians 6:10|Eph 6:10⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪besides⟫, ⟪moreover⟫, ⟪for the rest⟫: ⟦Philippians 3:1|Phl 3:1⟧ ⟦Philippians 4:8|4:8⟧; anarth., ⟦1 Corinthians 1:16|I Co 1:16⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 4:2|4:2⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 4:1|I Th 4:1⟧ (M, Th., in l; Lft., Notes, 51).

